// Rule 07: Account lockout on a non-machine account
// MITRE: Credential Access / T1110 (Brute Force)
// Severity: Medium (raise to High if the same account is locked out repeatedly)
// Schedule: every 15-30 min, lookback 1 h
// Entities: TargetUserName -> Account, TargetDomainName -> Host/NTDomain
// Incident grouping: one incident per TargetUserName
// Why: Rule 02 groups by source IP per hour and missed low-and-slow guessing spread over many IPs.
//   In the lab, azureuser was locked out 88 times (about 970 wrong passwords from 11 IPs), mostly below the per-IP threshold.
//   Lockout (4740) is the account-side signal and does not depend on the attacker's source IP.
// Note: 4740 carries the calling machine name, not the source IP. Correlate with 4625 (IpAddress) in the incident.
// Status: DRAFT - to be saved and backtested (expected hits: azureuser, Administrator, DefaultAccount, WDAGUtilityAccount)
let lookback = 1h;
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where EventID == 4740
| where TargetUserName !endswith "$"
| summarize Lockouts = count(),
            FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
            LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by TargetUserName, TargetDomainName, Computer
| project TargetUserName, TargetDomainName, Computer, Lockouts, FirstSeen, LastSeen
